out/
# Round reports are per-round artifacts: they quote session material and are
# not part of the shipped template. Keeping them out of git also keeps the
# no_internal_refs check meaningful for every file that is tracked.
ROUND-REPORT*.md
# The artifacts of a CI run. The workspace of a job holds the product
# configuration of the site, the file parameter of the pipeline, the
# console logs of the VMs and the scratch files of the tooling. They carry
# addresses and targets that belong to one site, they are never part of
# the template, and the leak check reads the tree and not the debris of a
# run.
product.conf
PRODUCT_CONF
console-logs/
.wtfbsd-*
